---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import Layout from '@/web/layouts/ContentLayout.astro';

const entries = (await getCollection('providers')).toSorted(
  (a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order
);
---

<Layout
  title="Claude Code providers: six integrations, eight templates"
  description="Compare six AI providers and eight templates for Claude Code: GLM, MiniMax, DeepSeek, Xiaomi MiMo, Kimi, and Qwen. Setup, pricing, and model details."
>
  <section class="relative z-10 pt-36 pb-12 px-6">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <h1
        class="reveal mt-5 text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.02em] leading-[1.05]"
      >
        Every provider claude-multi <span class="gradient-text">supports.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="reveal mt-5 text-text-dim max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed">
        claude-multi routes Claude Code to the provider you pick. Each provider
        exposes a native Anthropic-compatible endpoint, so setup is a single
        command. Each page below lists setup steps, pricing, and use cases.
      </p>
      <p class="reveal mt-4 text-text-mute text-sm font-mono">
        Six providers, eight templates. Last verified 2026-11-03.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="relative z-10 pb-12 px-6">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="reveal text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight mb-4">
        How to choose
      </h2>
      <p class="reveal text-text-dim max-w-3xl leading-relaxed">
        Start with how you pay. GLM is subscription-only: the Anthropic endpoint
        requires a Coding Plan, and there is no metered equivalent. DeepSeek and
        Kimi sell API tokens only. MiniMax sells both from the same URL, so the
        key type decides which quota is billed. MiMo and Qwen each have a second
        template for their subscription plans because those plans use a
        different endpoint, which is why six providers produce eight templates.
      </p>
      <p class="reveal mt-4 text-text-dim max-w-3xl leading-relaxed">
        Context is no longer the main filter. Every template now maps a
        1M-context model: GLM-5.3 and GLM-5.3-Flash, MiniMax-M3.1-Flash,
        DeepSeek Flash, MiMo V2.6, Kimi K3.1 Pro, and the Qwen 3.8 and 3.7
        models. Claude Code caps output at 128,000 tokens for these
        unrecognized model IDs, so larger model maximums do not change the
        practical ceiling.
      </p>
      <p class="reveal mt-4 text-text-dim max-w-3xl leading-relaxed">
        Price and plan coverage are the real differences. MiniMax and DeepSeek
        put a cheap Flash model in every slot. MiMo's Flash is cheaper still.
        Kimi charges flagship rates and offers Highspeed at double the price,
        so standard speed stays the default. Qwen's pay-as-you-go route reaches
        Qwen3.8-Max and Qwen3.8-Flash, while the Coding Plan covers only
        qwen3.7-plus among current Qwen models. GLM is a fixed credit plan.
        Pick the route that matches the models you need, not just the lowest
        headline rate.
      </p>
      <p class="reveal mt-4 text-text-dim max-w-3xl leading-relaxed">
        Then check geography. The MiMo Token Plan has CN, SG, and EU endpoints,
        and Qwen has separate international and China hosts. Pick the endpoint
        that matches your account and latency, not the one in the example.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="relative z-10 pb-32 px-6">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-4">
      {
        entries.map((entry) => (
          <a
            href={`/providers/${entry.id}/`}
            class="reveal block glass rounded-2xl p-7 no-underline transition-colors hover:border-edge-hover group"
          >
            <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-4 mb-3">
              <h2 class="text-xl font-bold tracking-tight group-hover:text-lime transition-colors">
                {entry.data.title}
              </h2>
              <span class="text-xs font-mono text-text-mute whitespace-nowrap mt-1">
                {entry.data.provider}
              </span>
            </div>
            <p class="text-text-dim leading-relaxed text-[0.95rem] mb-5">
              {entry.data.description}
            </p>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 flex-wrap">
              <code class="text-xs text-lime font-mono px-2.5 py-1 rounded-md border border-edge bg-[rgba(217,119,87,0.08)]">
                {entry.data.setupCommand}
              </code>
              <span class="text-xs font-mono text-text-mute">
                {entry.data.pricing}
              </span>
            </div>
          </a>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="relative z-10 pb-20 px-6">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight mb-6">
        Template reference
      </h2>
      <p class="text-text-dim mb-6 max-w-2xl">
        Each template pre-fills <code class="font-mono text-lime">ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL</code>,
        model mappings, and related env vars into your instance's <code class="font-mono text-lime">settings.json</code>.
        You only need to supply your API key.
      </p>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto glass rounded-2xl p-1 mb-10">
        <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
          <thead>
            <tr class="text-left text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-text-mute">
              <th class="p-3">Template</th>
              <th class="p-3">Display name</th>
              <th class="p-3">Endpoint</th>
              <th class="p-3">Opus model</th>
              <th class="p-3">Sonnet model</th>
              <th class="p-3">Fable model</th>
              <th class="p-3">Haiku model</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="text-text-dim">
            <tr class="border-t border-edge"><td class="p-3 font-mono text-lime">glm</td><td class="p-3">GLM Coding Plan</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">api.z.ai</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">glm-5.3[1m]</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">glm-5.3[1m]</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">glm-5.3[1m]</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">glm-5.3-flash[1m]</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-t border-edge"><td class="p-3 font-mono text-lime">minimax</td><td class="p-3">MiniMax</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">api.minimax.io</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">MiniMax-M3.1-Flash[1m]</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">MiniMax-M3.1-Flash[1m]</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">MiniMax-M3.1-Flash[1m]</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">MiniMax-M3.1-Flash[1m]</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-t border-edge"><td class="p-3 font-mono text-lime">deepseek</td><td class="p-3">DeepSeek</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">api.deepseek.com</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">deepseek-flash[1m]</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">deepseek-flash[1m]</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">deepseek-flash[1m]</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">deepseek-flash</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-t border-edge"><td class="p-3 font-mono text-lime">mimo</td><td class="p-3">Xiaomi MiMo</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">api.xiaomimimo.com</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">mimo-v2.6-pro[1m]</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">mimo-v2.6-pro[1m]</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">mimo-v2.6-pro[1m]</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">mimo-v2.6-flash[1m]</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-t border-edge"><td class="p-3 font-mono text-lime">mimo-token</td><td class="p-3">Xiaomi MiMo (Token Plan)</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">token-plan-cn.xiaomimimo.com</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">mimo-v2.6-pro[1m]</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">mimo-v2.6-pro[1m]</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">mimo-v2.6-pro[1m]</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">mimo-v2.6-flash[1m]</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-t border-edge"><td class="p-3 font-mono text-lime">kimi</td><td class="p-3">Moonshot Kimi</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">api.moonshot.ai</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">kimi-k3.1-pro[1m]</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">kimi-k3.1-pro[1m]</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">kimi-k3.1-pro[1m]</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">kimi-k3.1-pro[1m]</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-t border-edge"><td class="p-3 font-mono text-lime">qwen</td><td class="p-3">Alibaba Qwen</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">dashscope-intl.aliyuncs.com</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">qwen3.8-max</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">qwen3.7-plus</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">qwen3.8-max</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">qwen3.8-flash</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-t border-edge"><td class="p-3 font-mono text-lime">qwen-coding</td><td class="p-3">Alibaba Qwen Coding Plan</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">coding-intl.dashscope.aliyuncs.com</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">qwen3.7-plus</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">qwen3.7-plus</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">qwen3.7-plus</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">qwen3.7-plus</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <p class="text-text-dim text-sm max-w-3xl mb-10">
        The table reflects the current templates. Every template also maps the
        Fable alias to its primary model, and the effort-capable templates set
        <code class="font-mono text-lime text-xs">CLAUDE_CODE_ALWAYS_ENABLE_EFFORT=1</code>.
        Each provider page lists the live env vars and any manual options, such
        as DeepSeek V4-Pro.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-4">Pay per token vs. subscription</h3>
      <p class="text-text-dim mb-6 max-w-2xl">
        Some providers offer two access models, a pay-per-token API and a
        subscription/coding plan, each with a different base URL. Use the
        right template for your account type:
      </p>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto glass rounded-2xl p-1 mb-10">
        <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
          <thead>
            <tr class="text-left text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-text-mute">
              <th class="p-3">Provider</th>
              <th class="p-3">Pay-per-token template</th>
              <th class="p-3">Subscription template</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="text-text-dim">
            <tr class="border-t border-edge"><td class="p-3">Xiaomi MiMo</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">mimo</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">mimo-token (regional URL)</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-t border-edge"><td class="p-3">Alibaba Qwen</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">qwen</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">qwen-coding</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-t border-edge"><td class="p-3">GLM (Z.ai)</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">no pay-per-token template</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">glm (coding-plan-only)</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-t border-edge"><td class="p-3">MiniMax</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">minimax</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">same URL, different key type</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-t border-edge"><td class="p-3">Moonshot Kimi</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">kimi</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">pay per token only</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-t border-edge"><td class="p-3">DeepSeek</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">deepseek</td><td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs">pay per token only</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <ul class="text-text-dim text-sm space-y-2 max-w-2xl list-disc pl-5">
        <li>GLM: the Anthropic-compatible endpoint (<code class="font-mono text-lime text-xs">api.z.ai/api/anthropic</code>) is exclusive to the Z.ai Coding Plan subscription. The metered API only exposes an OpenAI-compatible URL. GLM-5.3 fills primary, opus, sonnet, and fable; GLM-5.3-Flash fills haiku. Both use the 1M hint and a 1M compaction window.</li>
        <li>DeepSeek: the template uses <code class="font-mono text-lime text-xs">deepseek-flash[1m]</code> in primary, opus, sonnet, and fable, and <code class="font-mono text-lime text-xs">deepseek-flash</code> in haiku and subagents. V4-Pro is the previous generation and remains a manual option. There is no released V4.1 Pro.</li>
        <li>MiMo Token Plan: defaults to the CN regional endpoint. If your subscription is SG or EU, update <code class="font-mono text-lime text-xs">ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL</code> with the endpoint shown in your subscription console. Both MiMo templates use the V2.6 model IDs.</li>
        <li>MiniMax: both plans use the same <code class="font-mono text-lime text-xs">api.minimax.io</code> endpoint; the API key type determines which quota is consumed. M3.1 Flash fills every slot, has a 1M token context window and a 512K output maximum, and always thinks. M3 remains available as the previous generation. M3.1 Flash costs $0.15/$0.60 per 1M tokens.</li>
        <li>Kimi: K2.5 was retired on 2026-08-31 and returns an error. K2.6 and K2.7 closed to new users on 2026-10-31 and retire by the end of December. The template uses K3.1 Pro in every slot at standard speed. Highspeed is optional and costs double. K3.1 Pro costs $2/$10 per 1M tokens.</li>
        <li>Qwen: pay-as-you-go uses Qwen3.8-Max, Qwen3.7-Plus, and Qwen3.8-Flash with a 983616 thinking-mode context setting and a 128000 output ceiling. The Coding Plan uses <code class="font-mono text-lime text-xs">qwen3.7-plus</code> in every slot and does not cover Qwen3.8-Max or Qwen3.8-Flash among current Qwen models. Qwen3-Coder-Next and Qwen3-Coder-Plus are not on the Anthropic-compatible matrix.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="relative z-10 px-6 pb-20">
    <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto reveal text-center">
      <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight">
        Set up your first instance
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-text-dim text-lg">
        The getting started guide walks through installing claude-multi and
        adding your first instance. It takes about two minutes.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-7 flex gap-3 justify-center flex-wrap">
        <a href="/docs/getting-started/" class="btn-primary">
          Get started
          <svg
            width="14"
            height="14"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2.5"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
            aria-hidden="true"
            ><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg
          >
        </a>
        <a href="/faq/" class="btn-secondary">Read the FAQ</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
